  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anticipatory action to mitigate effects of flooding and displacement in Lake Pro</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WASH and Shelter: &#x2022; Raising community awareness about the prevention of communicable diseases and promoting hygiene;  &#x2022; Distribution of hygiene kits and shelter kits;  &#x2022; Distribution of water treatment kits (PUR sachets, Aquatabs). Protection: Protection Activities &#x2022; Multi -sectoral Community Capacity Building: Child Protection (Training the community on specific risks and available support mechanisms. For example, how to identify signs of psychological distress in a child after an impending flood.) &#x2022; Organizing awareness sessions on social cohesion and peaceful coexistence  &#x2022; Prevention of Gender -Based Violence (GBV); Safety measures and referral pathways in case of flooding) Mapping of areas likely to be affected and analysis of probable referral pathways and safety measures.  &#x2022; Distribution of protection and dignity kits;  &#x2022; Risk analysis and implementation of mitigation measures: Safeguarding/Safeprogramming. &#x2022; Revitalizing accountability mechanisms adapted to all sensitive groups, including people with specific vulnerabilities: Receiving and processing feedback and complaints.</narrative>
  </description>
